# FinEra frontend (Vite) — optional overrides. Safe to omit: defaults use same-origin `/api/v1`.
#
# After git clone on any laptop (same GitHub account or not):
#   npm install
#   npm run dev          # Vite + backend-core (see package.json)
#   npm run dev:frontend # Vite only (backend must still be reachable — see below)
#
# Default (no VITE_API_URL): the browser calls `/api/v1` on whatever host serves the UI
# (localhost:5173 or http://THIS-PC-LAN-IP:5173). Vite proxies /api, /health, /ws to
# backend-core on this machine (vite.config.ts). Use that LAN URL from another device
# on the same Wi‑Fi; the dev server must run on the PC that hosts the API.
#
# If the API runs elsewhere (staging, tunnel, another PC), set full URLs:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-api.example.com/api/v1
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://your-api.example.com
#
# VITE_ENVIRONMENT=development
